1
00:00:54,453 --> 00:00:57,673
- They're on their way. Right now.
- They're here? Are they here?

2
00:01:39,772 --> 00:01:43,078
Say hello. This is CEO Han Jeong Yeon of HAN.

3
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:47,269
Nice to meet you.

4
00:01:47,269 --> 00:01:50,122
Welcome to APPELLO.

5
00:02:03,996 --> 00:02:07,782
Nice to meet you too, CEO Kang.

6
00:02:29,295 --> 00:02:31,532
Thank you for coming in person.

7
00:02:31,532 --> 00:02:35,296
You must be tired from the trip.
Please, come inside.

8
00:02:35,296 --> 00:02:37,296
I'll show you in.

9
00:02:38,892 --> 00:02:41,799
Right this way.

10
00:02:41,799 --> 00:02:43,939
Watch your step.

11
00:02:56,294 --> 00:02:59,000
She's gorgeous.

12
00:03:04,454 --> 00:03:09,244
I was very impressed by APPELLO's proposal.

13
00:03:09,244 --> 00:03:12,223
That's why I wanted to come see it for myself.

14
00:03:17,284 --> 00:03:22,988
At HAN, we've shortlisted SE:ON and APPELLO

15
00:03:22,988 --> 00:03:25,830
and we'll be giving
both companies the same task.

16
00:03:26,856 --> 00:03:28,194
Sorry?

17
00:03:28,857 --> 00:03:30,328
It's simple.

18
00:03:30,328 --> 00:03:33,648
"Who is HAN's customer?"

19
00:03:33,648 --> 00:03:35,425
That's what we want you to define.

20
00:03:35,425 --> 00:03:40,118
So you want us to profile the target customer?

21
00:03:40,118 --> 00:03:41,255
Exactly.

22
00:03:41,255 --> 00:03:45,528
We'll make our final decision
after both companies present.

23
00:03:49,916 --> 00:03:52,436
Man... This won't be easy.

24
00:04:00,757 --> 00:04:02,530
[Episode 10]

25
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:09,716
So what am I supposed to make of this?

26
00:04:11,484 --> 00:04:14,108
I happened to run into her recently.

27
00:04:14,108 --> 00:04:16,919
You said you wanted to see APPELLO,
so I showed you around,

28
00:04:16,919 --> 00:04:19,910
and now you pull this on me?

29
00:04:19,910 --> 00:04:22,297
Business is business.

30
00:04:23,916 --> 00:04:27,930
I only told Chan today that I'm the CEO of HAN.

31
00:04:31,001 --> 00:04:32,939
Anyway...

32
00:04:32,939 --> 00:04:36,908
It's nice having the three of us
together again.

33
00:04:42,215 --> 00:04:44,632
You two CEOs can keep talking.

34
00:04:44,632 --> 00:04:46,998
I have a schedule.

35
00:05:02,107 --> 00:05:05,838
I'm surprised HAN's CEO came in person.

36
00:05:05,838 --> 00:05:08,013
That's unusual.

37
00:05:08,013 --> 00:05:11,611
Didn't something seem off earlier?

38
00:05:11,611 --> 00:05:13,911
What? How?

39
00:05:14,613 --> 00:05:16,671
- CEO Kang's expression...
- Yeah?

40
00:05:16,671 --> 00:05:21,984
It looked like they already knew each other.

41
00:05:26,967 --> 00:05:29,971
<i>Who directs this store?</i>

42
00:05:29,971 --> 00:05:32,944
<i>It's good to see you too, CEO Kang.</i>

43
00:05:48,059 --> 00:05:50,129
<i>Who's this?</i>

44
00:05:50,129 --> 00:05:53,355
<i>The woman from that photo?</i>

45
00:05:54,715 --> 00:05:58,695
You still come and go as you please.

46
00:06:04,371 --> 00:06:06,657
You really haven't changed.

47
00:06:08,417 --> 00:06:10,692
Have dinner with me.

48
00:06:11,992 --> 00:06:14,138
I already have plans.

49
00:06:15,732 --> 00:06:18,412
I'm asking as CEO of HAN.

50
00:06:26,027 --> 00:06:28,653
There's something important I need to tell you.

51
00:06:37,657 --> 00:06:39,214
<i>Sorry, Ms. Nam.</i>

52
00:06:39,214 --> 00:06:42,835
<i>My meeting with the HAN's CEO might run long.</i>

53
00:06:42,835 --> 00:06:44,835
<i>What should we do?</i>

54
00:06:47,982 --> 00:06:49,212
<i>No worries.</i>

55
00:06:49,212 --> 00:06:52,052
<i>It's important for the company,
so that comes first.</i>

56
00:06:52,052 --> 00:06:54,212
<i>I understand.</i>

57
00:06:57,995 --> 00:06:59,573
Come on...

58
00:06:59,573 --> 00:07:03,232
I was so excited to meet your first boyfriend.

59
00:07:03,232 --> 00:07:05,716
Canceling last minute is pretty harsh.

60
00:07:05,716 --> 00:07:08,309
It's a really important meeting.

61
00:07:08,309 --> 00:07:10,551
Cut him some slack.

62
00:07:10,551 --> 00:07:11,596
- What?
- Oh my!

63
00:07:11,596 --> 00:07:13,668
Ha Gi can't make it tonight?

64
00:07:13,668 --> 00:07:14,706
Hi.

65
00:07:14,706 --> 00:07:16,168
Oh, come on.

66
00:07:16,168 --> 00:07:18,587
I was going to introduce myself too.

67
00:07:18,587 --> 00:07:20,087
Why would you?

68
00:07:20,087 --> 00:07:21,997
You're Da Reum's friend.

69
00:07:21,997 --> 00:07:23,244
I'm Ha Gi's friend.

70
00:07:23,244 --> 00:07:25,268
Da Reum and Ha Gi are dating.

71
00:07:25,268 --> 00:07:27,108
And you and I are basically...

72
00:07:27,108 --> 00:07:29,768
Instructor and student, aren't we?

73
00:07:31,494 --> 00:07:34,479
Then dinner's on me tonight.

74
00:07:34,479 --> 00:07:36,496
- What do you want to eat?
- What?

75
00:07:36,496 --> 00:07:38,789
Pick whatever you want.

76
00:07:38,789 --> 00:07:41,042
- Excuse me!
- Oh my...

77
00:07:41,042 --> 00:07:42,204
What should we order?

78
00:07:42,204 --> 00:07:44,647
- Can we order a lot, then?
- Of course. Just name it.

79
00:07:46,779 --> 00:07:50,586
I thought you'd be happier to see me.

80
00:07:52,673 --> 00:07:55,459
Not exactly fond memories.

81
00:07:58,845 --> 00:08:00,832
I found out later.

82
00:08:49,861 --> 00:08:51,948
<i>Lee Chan!</i>

83
00:08:58,503 --> 00:09:01,987
The reason he left to become a trainee...

84
00:09:01,987 --> 00:09:04,063
was because of us.

85
00:09:05,419 --> 00:09:07,343
Back then...

86
00:09:07,343 --> 00:09:10,083
I lost my best friend.

87
00:09:12,743 --> 00:09:15,723
He came back eventually, but even now...

88
00:09:17,650 --> 00:09:20,176
Chan and I never talk about it.

89
00:09:22,250 --> 00:09:24,634
Then you left to study abroad
without saying a word,

90
00:09:24,634 --> 00:09:26,940
and I was left all alone.

91
00:09:27,843 --> 00:09:30,256
How could that be a good memory?

92
00:09:31,777 --> 00:09:34,417
You're right.

93
00:09:34,417 --> 00:09:37,276
I should've told you before I left.

94
00:09:38,903 --> 00:09:41,343
Was it hard on you?

95
00:09:45,557 --> 00:09:48,257
Were we even that serious?

96
00:09:49,884 --> 00:09:52,257
We only dated for a few months.

97
00:09:56,445 --> 00:09:58,388
I...

98
00:09:58,388 --> 00:10:00,864
Sometimes, when I thought of Korea...

99
00:10:01,718 --> 00:10:04,024
I thought of you.

100
00:10:06,437 --> 00:10:09,771
So what did you want to tell me as CEO?

101
00:10:16,909 --> 00:10:19,286
Wait, who?

102
00:10:19,286 --> 00:10:20,746
Han Jeong Yeon?

103
00:10:20,746 --> 00:10:22,471
She really came here?

104
00:10:22,471 --> 00:10:25,663
So she wasn't your classmate.
She was an upperclassman.

105
00:10:25,663 --> 00:10:28,206
Yeah. One year ahead of us.

106
00:10:28,206 --> 00:10:30,176
This just got interesting.

107
00:10:30,176 --> 00:10:33,693
Jeong Yeon was Ha Gi's first love.

108
00:10:33,693 --> 00:10:36,904
Back then, every guy had a crush on her.

109
00:10:36,904 --> 00:10:39,490
Even Chan liked her.

110
00:10:41,146 --> 00:10:44,152
She was basically everyone's first love.

111
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:46,818
That's wild.

112
00:10:46,818 --> 00:10:49,803
How do they end up meeting again like this?

113
00:10:54,707 --> 00:10:57,532
So... she was his first love?

114
00:10:57,532 --> 00:10:58,694
Yeah.

115
00:10:59,628 --> 00:11:00,666
Come on.

116
00:11:00,666 --> 00:11:03,032
That was ages ago.

117
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:06,377
Jeong Yeon's still gorgeous, right?

118
00:11:06,377 --> 00:11:08,101
If I ran into my first love again...

119
00:11:08,101 --> 00:11:11,041
I don't think my heart could take it.

120
00:11:14,739 --> 00:11:17,102
- How about a toast?
- All right, glasses up!

121
00:11:17,102 --> 00:11:19,412
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

122
00:11:30,417 --> 00:11:31,949
[HAN made not a brand, but an aesthetic]

123
00:11:31,949 --> 00:11:32,804
[Four Key Insights on HAN]

124
00:11:32,804 --> 00:11:37,766
SE's proposal and APPELLO's were very similar.

125
00:11:37,766 --> 00:11:41,053
That's no coincidence, right?

126
00:11:44,561 --> 00:11:47,443
There's a mole inside.

127
00:11:47,443 --> 00:11:48,868
I'm trying to find them.

128
00:11:48,868 --> 00:11:50,875
I knew something was off.

129
00:11:51,844 --> 00:11:54,370
Any suspects?

130
00:11:55,238 --> 00:11:56,868
Not yet.

131
00:11:58,338 --> 00:12:00,338
Nothing solid.

132
00:12:03,391 --> 00:12:08,846
I thought we might want the same thing.

133
00:12:11,433 --> 00:12:14,823
I didn't come here to sign with SE.

134
00:12:14,823 --> 00:12:17,179
I came for revenge.

135
00:12:28,597 --> 00:12:32,407
<i>I get my revenge. You find your mole.</i>

136
00:12:32,407 --> 00:12:35,810
<i>If we team up, we both win.</i>

137
00:12:36,450 --> 00:12:38,923
<i>Think about it.</i>

138
00:12:48,461 --> 00:12:51,385
Hey, you're his girlfriend now!

139
00:12:51,385 --> 00:12:53,826
And you're a catch.

140
00:12:53,826 --> 00:12:56,304
First love? Who cares?

141
00:12:56,304 --> 00:12:58,295
- She doesn't stand a chance!
- Not a chance!

142
00:12:58,295 --> 00:12:59,759
Well... maybe she has a shot.

143
00:12:59,759 --> 00:13:01,008
Come on!

144
00:13:01,765 --> 00:13:03,888
She is gorgeous, though.

145
00:13:03,888 --> 00:13:07,708
Hey, student. Be quiet.

146
00:13:07,708 --> 00:13:11,426
Who does your boyfriend like now?

147
00:13:11,426 --> 00:13:12,452
You!

148
00:13:12,452 --> 00:13:14,658
Exactly! You!

149
00:13:17,365 --> 00:13:18,685
Right!

150
00:13:18,685 --> 00:13:20,962
- Right!
- Right!

151
00:13:20,962 --> 00:13:22,772
- You!
- Yeah...

152
00:13:22,772 --> 00:13:24,562
Instructor and student...

153
00:13:24,562 --> 00:13:26,895
He likes me. Of course.

154
00:13:26,895 --> 00:13:29,984
Just instructor and student.

155
00:13:29,984 --> 00:13:32,444
Right... of course.

156
00:13:43,303 --> 00:13:45,299
Sorry I'm late.

157
00:13:47,350 --> 00:13:49,916
How did you make it?

158
00:13:50,776 --> 00:13:53,140
I'll drink this as my penalty for being late.

159
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:54,513
You better!

160
00:14:06,495 --> 00:14:08,221
Let's go!

161
00:14:11,661 --> 00:14:13,814
We're going for round two, right?

162
00:14:15,255 --> 00:14:16,619
We'll head out first.

163
00:14:16,619 --> 00:14:19,303
I'll make it up to you
with a proper dinner next time.

164
00:14:19,303 --> 00:14:21,876
Hey, man!

165
00:14:29,276 --> 00:14:31,182
I'm watching you.

166
00:14:32,004 --> 00:14:38,147
If you ever make Da Reum cry,
you'll have me to answer to.

167
00:14:38,147 --> 00:14:39,787
Got it?

168
00:14:40,392 --> 00:14:42,465
Got it?

169
00:14:43,759 --> 00:14:45,620
Okay.

170
00:14:45,620 --> 00:14:48,620
Da Reum, let's go.

171
00:14:49,762 --> 00:14:52,066
- Bye, guys.
- Bye!

172
00:14:52,066 --> 00:14:53,237
Bye!

173
00:14:53,237 --> 00:14:55,874
- Want to go for round two?
- No. Go home.

174
00:14:55,874 --> 00:14:59,156
Come on! No round two?

175
00:14:59,156 --> 00:15:00,548
Mi Mi!

176
00:15:09,229 --> 00:15:11,246
Mi Mi.

177
00:15:11,246 --> 00:15:16,075
I really thought we had something going on.

178
00:15:16,735 --> 00:15:19,135
Min Woo.

179
00:15:19,135 --> 00:15:20,863
Do you really like me?

180
00:15:20,863 --> 00:15:22,782
I fell for you at first sight.

181
00:15:22,782 --> 00:15:26,196
When I'm working, eating, even showering...

182
00:15:26,196 --> 00:15:30,322
Even when I'm on the toilet,
all I think about is you.

183
00:15:34,306 --> 00:15:40,092
I can't get you out of my head.

184
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:49,653
Remember what I said my type was?

185
00:15:49,653 --> 00:15:51,607
Your type?

186
00:15:51,607 --> 00:15:55,471
Someone capable and a good kisser?

187
00:15:55,471 --> 00:15:57,911
I don't like guys who can't kiss.

188
00:16:43,815 --> 00:16:45,572
Did we really just do that?

189
00:16:45,572 --> 00:16:48,745
Oh my God! That was amazing!

190
00:16:48,745 --> 00:16:50,625
See you tomorrow, Mi Mi!

191
00:17:01,023 --> 00:17:03,143
I'm okay now.

192
00:17:06,823 --> 00:17:09,622
Are you mad I broke our plans?

193
00:17:10,296 --> 00:17:11,807
No.

194
00:17:11,807 --> 00:17:15,013
I'm not that petty.

195
00:17:15,890 --> 00:17:18,722
Then why are you pouting?

196
00:17:22,462 --> 00:17:25,868
I heard you and CEO Han used to be close.

197
00:17:25,868 --> 00:17:27,714
Back in high school.

198
00:17:28,874 --> 00:17:30,900
Well... yeah.

199
00:17:31,534 --> 00:17:33,747
We were close.

200
00:17:35,388 --> 00:17:37,807
That's all?

201
00:17:39,508 --> 00:17:41,941
That's all.

202
00:17:48,537 --> 00:17:51,517
Damn you, Kim Min Woo.

203
00:17:51,517 --> 00:17:52,674
Ms. Nam.

204
00:17:52,674 --> 00:17:53,987
Ms. Nam.

205
00:17:53,987 --> 00:17:57,340
I heard she was your first love.

206
00:17:57,340 --> 00:18:00,275
- Well, that...
- Were you happy to see her again?

207
00:18:00,275 --> 00:18:02,299
Enough to be late for our plans?

208
00:18:02,299 --> 00:18:04,107
Don't get the wrong idea.

209
00:18:04,107 --> 00:18:06,600
That was a long time ago.

210
00:18:08,034 --> 00:18:11,927
She had a proposal for me,
so the meeting ran long.

211
00:18:12,640 --> 00:18:15,173
What kind of proposal?

212
00:18:18,487 --> 00:18:21,037
It's very important to APPELLO.

213
00:18:21,037 --> 00:18:24,391
I can't tell you everything yet.
It's sensitive.

214
00:18:24,391 --> 00:18:27,237
But I won't lie to you.

215
00:18:28,058 --> 00:18:31,177
Can you wait a little longer?

216
00:18:34,866 --> 00:18:37,405
And don't worry.

217
00:18:43,608 --> 00:18:49,374
You're the one I like now.

218
00:18:52,629 --> 00:18:55,626
I know, but...

219
00:18:55,626 --> 00:18:57,623
Trust me.

220
00:18:57,623 --> 00:18:59,346
Okay?

221
00:19:34,263 --> 00:19:35,463
[Han Jeong Yeon]

222
00:19:36,421 --> 00:19:37,460
<i>Yeah.</i>

223
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:40,273
I just left Ha Gi.

224
00:19:40,273 --> 00:19:42,324
What were you two talking about this late?

225
00:19:42,324 --> 00:19:44,913
Just old times.

226
00:19:45,533 --> 00:19:48,244
You told me to go after him, right?

227
00:19:48,244 --> 00:19:50,244
So?

228
00:19:50,942 --> 00:19:53,267
It bruised my ego.

229
00:19:53,267 --> 00:19:56,853
I mean, I'm his first love,
and he barely reacted.

230
00:19:56,853 --> 00:19:59,926
<i>I think I'll push a little harder.</i>

231
00:20:01,446 --> 00:20:03,303
What do you mean?

232
00:20:03,303 --> 00:20:04,488
<i>Why?</i>

233
00:20:04,488 --> 00:20:07,406
<i>Isn't that what you wanted?</i>

234
00:20:07,406 --> 00:20:10,430
<i>Don't feel too guilty.</i>

235
00:20:10,430 --> 00:20:12,477
Because now...

236
00:20:12,477 --> 00:20:17,310
I want Ha Gi back.

237
00:20:32,397 --> 00:20:34,034
[If You Don't Know HAN, You Don't Know Fashion]

238
00:20:34,034 --> 00:20:35,040
[A Gen Z Fashion Sensation]

239
00:20:40,250 --> 00:20:42,501
[Clothes that stay with you]

240
00:20:45,737 --> 00:20:47,990
"Clothes that stay with you."

241
00:21:13,192 --> 00:21:15,110
A dedicated point person?

242
00:21:15,110 --> 00:21:19,214
Yeah. I can't exactly call the CEO
every time something comes up.

243
00:21:19,214 --> 00:21:23,670
You said Ms. Nam wrote the proposal, right?

244
00:21:25,350 --> 00:21:27,536
I want her as my point person.

245
00:21:33,027 --> 00:21:34,616
Why her, of all people?

246
00:21:34,616 --> 00:21:36,237
I told you.

247
00:21:36,237 --> 00:21:38,728
I liked APPELLO's proposal.

248
00:21:38,728 --> 00:21:42,309
She clearly understands our brand.

249
00:21:43,850 --> 00:21:47,080
I'll ask if she's interested.

250
00:21:47,080 --> 00:21:49,136
Why not ask her now?

251
00:21:58,097 --> 00:22:00,097
Ms. Nam?

252
00:22:02,822 --> 00:22:03,861
Yes?

253
00:22:03,861 --> 00:22:06,181
I read your proposal.

254
00:22:06,181 --> 00:22:08,902
I need someone from APPELLO
to handle things with us.

255
00:22:08,902 --> 00:22:12,782
Would you be interested in taking it on?

256
00:22:17,297 --> 00:22:20,584
If you're okay with me...

257
00:22:21,747 --> 00:22:24,485
It is a good opportunity, but...

258
00:22:24,485 --> 00:22:27,181
what matters most is what you want.

259
00:22:28,500 --> 00:22:30,692
What do you think?

260
00:22:33,193 --> 00:22:34,999
Then...

261
00:22:36,246 --> 00:22:38,619
I'd like to give it a try.

262
00:22:39,744 --> 00:22:41,768
Great.

263
00:22:41,768 --> 00:22:43,838
I'm counting on you.

264
00:23:02,119 --> 00:23:05,213
<i>Don't feel too guilty.</i>

265
00:23:05,213 --> 00:23:07,236
<i>Because...</i>

266
00:23:07,236 --> 00:23:11,899
<i>I want Ha Gi back.</i>

267
00:23:20,603 --> 00:23:21,605
[Won Bin]

268
00:23:23,006 --> 00:23:24,049
Hey.

269
00:23:24,049 --> 00:23:26,902
<i>Chan! We've got a problem.</i>

270
00:23:31,095 --> 00:23:33,108
Hey.

271
00:23:33,108 --> 00:23:34,661
Let's go.

272
00:23:36,729 --> 00:23:38,446
Here. Put this on first.

273
00:23:38,446 --> 00:23:40,976
No. I didn't do anything wrong.

274
00:23:40,976 --> 00:23:44,713
You don't have any weird photos
or videos on there, do you?

275
00:23:44,713 --> 00:23:46,973
Come on. What do you take me for?

276
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:51,291
But Jinu and Teo were the ones
who got hacked.

277
00:23:51,291 --> 00:23:54,289
Why are they calling you in too?

278
00:23:54,289 --> 00:23:56,685
This is freaking me out.

279
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:58,574
There it is.

280
00:24:00,146 --> 00:24:02,293
[Investigation Division]

281
00:24:02,293 --> 00:24:06,131
We caught the hacker before anything leaked.

282
00:24:06,131 --> 00:24:08,461
Among the files used for the blackmail,

283
00:24:08,461 --> 00:24:13,274
we found unreleased songs and videos
involving you.

284
00:24:13,274 --> 00:24:15,407
We called you in to verify that.

285
00:24:18,203 --> 00:24:19,446
Wait.

286
00:24:19,446 --> 00:24:22,465
These are files for an album.

287
00:24:22,465 --> 00:24:25,206
You were all working on it.

288
00:24:25,858 --> 00:24:27,615
It must've meant a lot to them.

289
00:24:27,615 --> 00:24:32,028
They even paid the hacker
to keep it from leaking.

290
00:24:35,217 --> 00:24:38,043
Why would they go this far?

291
00:24:39,070 --> 00:24:41,476
Those idiots. They didn't tell me a thing.

292
00:24:52,423 --> 00:24:54,349
Guys.

293
00:24:57,682 --> 00:24:59,302
Hey.

294
00:25:12,611 --> 00:25:15,528
You should've called me
the second this happened.

295
00:25:15,528 --> 00:25:19,476
What money do you even have
to pay off a hacker?

296
00:25:19,476 --> 00:25:22,278
Your files were in there too.

297
00:25:23,304 --> 00:25:25,022
And the songs we worked on for years...

298
00:25:25,022 --> 00:25:26,536
We broke up ten years ago.

299
00:25:26,536 --> 00:25:28,745
Why are you still doing this?

300
00:25:28,745 --> 00:25:30,492
Live your own lives. Please.

301
00:25:30,492 --> 00:25:33,819
It may be over for you,
but it's not over for us!

302
00:25:33,819 --> 00:25:35,695
To us...

303
00:25:35,695 --> 00:25:38,208
DNX is everything.

304
00:25:40,617 --> 00:25:42,409
I'm sorry.

305
00:25:42,409 --> 00:25:45,769
We'll make sure
we don't get in your way anymore.

306
00:25:46,889 --> 00:25:48,773
Hey, Jinu!

307
00:25:48,773 --> 00:25:50,615
Jinu!

308
00:26:07,696 --> 00:26:10,059
I know you're both busy
preparing your presentations,

309
00:26:10,059 --> 00:26:13,193
so I thought I'd treat you both
to a meal and cheer you on.

310
00:26:13,193 --> 00:26:15,217
We hardly need cheering on.

311
00:26:15,217 --> 00:26:18,368
We're already right on APPELLO's heels
after launching our platform.

312
00:26:18,368 --> 00:26:21,588
It's only a matter of time
before we take first place.

313
00:26:21,588 --> 00:26:26,408
We've almost finished
profiling the customer too.

314
00:26:26,408 --> 00:26:31,254
HAN customers are ultimately drawn
to exclusivity, aren't they?

315
00:26:39,429 --> 00:26:44,272
<i>Aren't HAN customers drawn to exclusivity?</i>

316
00:26:44,272 --> 00:26:47,689
<i>That desire to have what others can't.</i>

317
00:26:47,689 --> 00:26:48,902
<i>Right.</i>

318
00:26:48,902 --> 00:26:51,995
<i>You can see it
from all those opening-day lines.</i>

319
00:27:05,806 --> 00:27:07,656
Exclusivity.

320
00:27:07,656 --> 00:27:12,069
We should use a limited-edition strategy
in Korea too.

321
00:27:12,752 --> 00:27:15,289
Interesting take.

322
00:27:15,289 --> 00:27:19,295
What about APPELLO?

323
00:27:23,636 --> 00:27:26,070
Well...

324
00:27:26,070 --> 00:27:30,016
We're still working it out.

325
00:27:36,318 --> 00:27:38,271
Come on. Let's eat.

326
00:27:39,864 --> 00:27:41,657
Thank you.

327
00:28:00,743 --> 00:28:01,768
Hey.

328
00:28:01,768 --> 00:28:04,248
There's definitely something going on
between CEO Kang and Han.

329
00:28:04,248 --> 00:28:06,881
Find out what it is.

330
00:28:20,345 --> 00:28:22,404
Still here?

331
00:28:23,877 --> 00:28:25,804
Director Lee.

332
00:28:30,590 --> 00:28:33,067
I was passing by
and saw the lights were still on.

333
00:28:33,067 --> 00:28:36,564
Of course it'd be you working this late.

334
00:28:36,564 --> 00:28:39,703
I just have a few things to wrap up.

335
00:28:39,703 --> 00:28:42,190
Don't you have a date or something?

336
00:28:46,354 --> 00:28:48,470
I know, right?

337
00:28:53,952 --> 00:28:56,605
Have you eaten anything?

338
00:29:01,490 --> 00:29:03,490
Earlier...

339
00:29:04,111 --> 00:29:07,201
I saw Jinu and Teo at the police station.

340
00:29:07,201 --> 00:29:09,711
The police station?

341
00:29:09,711 --> 00:29:12,741
They got hacked,

342
00:29:12,741 --> 00:29:15,800
and all the files were for a DNX comeback.

343
00:29:18,022 --> 00:29:20,689
They still haven't given up on that dream.

344
00:29:22,063 --> 00:29:24,845
I didn't know they wanted it that badly.

345
00:29:28,308 --> 00:29:30,908
You feel the same way, right?

346
00:29:32,241 --> 00:29:36,548
Isn't that why you've kept writing songs
for the fans?

347
00:29:42,237 --> 00:29:44,590
Yeah.

348
00:29:47,964 --> 00:29:50,413
But I guess I'm not brave enough.

349
00:29:50,413 --> 00:29:55,351
A great opportunity, my career...

350
00:29:55,351 --> 00:29:57,884
I don't have the courage
to walk away from all that.

351
00:29:59,420 --> 00:30:02,852
Because... that's the practical choice?

352
00:30:13,037 --> 00:30:15,983
I should focus on the movie for now, right?

353
00:30:21,490 --> 00:30:24,140
Whatever you decide...

354
00:30:24,140 --> 00:30:29,080
I hope you choose something
you truly want to do.

355
00:30:30,584 --> 00:30:32,943
Just for yourself.

356
00:30:49,499 --> 00:30:51,357
<i>Whatever you decide...</i>

357
00:30:51,357 --> 00:30:55,903
<i>I hope you choose something
you truly want to do.</i>

358
00:30:55,903 --> 00:30:58,343
<i>Just for yourself.</i>

359
00:31:40,870 --> 00:31:42,528
Ms. Nam.

360
00:31:42,528 --> 00:31:44,083
Look.

361
00:31:52,780 --> 00:31:54,937
What's this?

362
00:31:54,937 --> 00:31:56,251
It's so pretty.

363
00:31:56,251 --> 00:31:58,378
What is all this?

364
00:31:58,378 --> 00:32:01,144
Oh my! Did you set this up?

365
00:32:05,485 --> 00:32:07,328
It's so pretty.

366
00:32:07,328 --> 00:32:10,028
When did you have time to plan all this?

367
00:32:10,965 --> 00:32:14,631
I'd seen this place before and just thought...

368
00:32:15,758 --> 00:32:17,544
Really?

369
00:32:20,218 --> 00:32:22,331
Try this.

370
00:32:27,469 --> 00:32:29,762
- Good?
- So good.

371
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:48,102
Weekends are way too short.

372
00:32:50,422 --> 00:32:52,719
I don't want to go to work tomorrow.

373
00:32:56,726 --> 00:32:59,252
Is that something you say to your CEO?

374
00:33:02,259 --> 00:33:04,672
I was saying it to my boyfriend.

375
00:33:29,837 --> 00:33:31,340
[4:00 PM - Head to the lake]
[5:00 PM - Sunset shimmer]

376
00:33:37,243 --> 00:33:39,000
Want to go down to the lake?

377
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:40,193
Why?

378
00:33:40,193 --> 00:33:41,690
Well...

379
00:33:41,690 --> 00:33:43,643
I heard it's beautiful around sunset.

380
00:33:43,643 --> 00:33:46,083
You wanted to show me the sunset on the water?

381
00:33:47,836 --> 00:33:51,136
I'd rather stay here a little longer.

382
00:34:06,832 --> 00:34:09,965
[3:00 PM - Picnic on the lawn]
[4:00 PM - Head to the lake]

383
00:34:12,880 --> 00:34:15,740
We don't have to do everything you planned.

384
00:34:17,842 --> 00:34:20,949
Why are you trying so hard today?

385
00:34:23,239 --> 00:34:27,298
I didn't get to properly meet
your friends last time,

386
00:34:28,643 --> 00:34:30,020
and we haven't seen each other lately.

387
00:34:30,020 --> 00:34:32,229
Was that bothering you?

388
00:34:34,803 --> 00:34:38,563
I wanted to do it right this time.

389
00:34:39,963 --> 00:34:41,987
Or more specifically...

390
00:34:41,987 --> 00:34:44,253
this is because of CEO Han, isn't it?

391
00:34:49,122 --> 00:34:52,596
- Well, that...
- You said I had nothing to worry about.

392
00:34:52,596 --> 00:34:55,001
I trust you.

393
00:34:55,001 --> 00:34:58,190
That's why I agreed to take on the HAN account.

394
00:34:58,190 --> 00:35:00,000
You don't have to keep doing more.

395
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:02,356
I just like being with you.

396
00:35:13,084 --> 00:35:15,084
Thank you.

397
00:35:18,800 --> 00:35:20,538
Want to lie back down?

398
00:35:20,538 --> 00:35:24,180
- I want to stay like this a little longer.
- Okay.

399
00:35:39,481 --> 00:35:41,147
Sorry.

400
00:35:42,774 --> 00:35:46,292
Man, it's been so long,
I barely remember any of this.

401
00:35:46,292 --> 00:35:48,739
You're getting old.

402
00:35:48,739 --> 00:35:49,983
Wait till you're my age.

403
00:35:49,983 --> 00:35:52,383
Moving like this isn't as easy as it looks.

404
00:35:52,383 --> 00:35:53,700
Anyway...

405
00:35:53,700 --> 00:35:55,723
It feels so good practicing together again.

406
00:35:55,723 --> 00:35:57,201
- Same here.
- Why are you getting all mushy?

407
00:35:57,201 --> 00:35:59,707
Get away from me.

408
00:35:59,707 --> 00:36:02,627
I wish Chan were here too.

409
00:36:10,063 --> 00:36:13,139
Don't get your hopes up.

410
00:36:13,139 --> 00:36:16,539
Why would a top star still care about DNX?

411
00:36:16,539 --> 00:36:19,119
He's about to go Hollywood.

412
00:36:20,752 --> 00:36:23,015
Let's go again, okay?

413
00:36:23,015 --> 00:36:24,330
From "Get On."

414
00:36:38,108 --> 00:36:40,027
[Myungmyung Building]

415
00:37:20,156 --> 00:37:22,156
<i>Roy.</i>

416
00:37:23,789 --> 00:37:26,848
<i>I don't care who you like.</i>

417
00:37:27,649 --> 00:37:29,740
<i>But...</i>

418
00:37:29,740 --> 00:37:32,853
<i>this is too much for us to handle right now.</i>

419
00:37:34,639 --> 00:37:36,599
<i>Let's keep it quiet.</i>

420
00:37:37,385 --> 00:37:39,366
<i>Later...</i>

421
00:37:40,006 --> 00:37:42,585
<i>when we're in a better place...</i>

422
00:37:43,812 --> 00:37:45,779
<i>just until then.</i>

423
00:37:50,636 --> 00:37:52,636
<i>Okay.</i>

424
00:38:01,942 --> 00:38:05,455
[DNX's Roy:
Private Photos With Same-Sex Partner Leaked]

425
00:38:08,403 --> 00:38:11,113
[DNX's Rapid Rise Hits Sudden Roadblock]
[All Eyes on What Comes Next]

426
00:38:11,113 --> 00:38:13,623
<i>Stop looking at it.</i>

427
00:38:13,623 --> 00:38:17,129
<i>- What do we do now?
- If only you'd been...</i>

428
00:38:18,622 --> 00:38:21,535
<i>a little more careful, Roy.</i>

429
00:38:26,236 --> 00:38:27,632
<i>Stop!</i>

430
00:38:27,632 --> 00:38:29,559
<i>- Don't do that to Roy!
- Hey!</i>

431
00:38:29,559 --> 00:38:30,657
<i>- Stop!
- Move!</i>

432
00:38:30,657 --> 00:38:32,236
<i>- Get out of the way!
- You can't turn on him too!</i>

433
00:38:32,236 --> 00:38:34,236
<i>I said move!</i>

434
00:38:35,149 --> 00:38:36,826
<i>That goes for you too.</i>

435
00:38:36,826 --> 00:38:39,449
<i>You two ruined everything we worked for!</i>

436
00:39:02,882 --> 00:39:04,066
Great work today!

437
00:39:04,066 --> 00:39:06,553
- Good job.
- Thanks.

438
00:39:06,553 --> 00:39:09,898
Hey, the boss saw him,
and swears he's really a celebrity.

439
00:39:09,898 --> 00:39:12,056
That D... DN...

440
00:39:12,056 --> 00:39:14,494
- What was it called again?
- No way.

441
00:39:14,494 --> 00:39:17,403
I'm telling you, it's true!

442
00:39:17,403 --> 00:39:18,690
- Fifty thousand won says he is.
- Fifty thousand?

443
00:39:18,690 --> 00:39:20,586
- Yeah.
- Deal.

444
00:39:20,586 --> 00:39:22,679
No backing out, okay?

445
00:39:28,312 --> 00:39:31,334
Hey, take off your helmet.

446
00:39:31,334 --> 00:39:34,193
You've worked here for months
and we've never seen your face.

447
00:39:34,193 --> 00:39:36,203
I heard you used to be an idol. Is that true?

448
00:39:36,203 --> 00:39:37,310
- No.
- Come on, let us see.

449
00:39:37,310 --> 00:39:39,987
- I'm not.
- Just take it off.

450
00:39:39,987 --> 00:39:42,106
- Come on.
- Let us see.

451
00:39:45,327 --> 00:39:49,187
You guys have way too much time on your hands.

452
00:39:50,627 --> 00:39:53,297
It's peak delivery time.

453
00:39:53,297 --> 00:39:54,772
What are you all doing?

454
00:39:54,772 --> 00:39:56,477
Who are you?

455
00:40:00,371 --> 00:40:02,396
Delivery pay is triple right now.

456
00:40:02,396 --> 00:40:04,407
There's a limited-time promo.

457
00:40:04,407 --> 00:40:05,829
[TRIPLE DELIVERY PAY!]
[ONLY TWO HOURS!]

458
00:40:07,901 --> 00:40:10,757
We'll check when we get back!

459
00:40:10,757 --> 00:40:13,583
It's only for two hours.

460
00:40:16,461 --> 00:40:18,527
What a bunch of jerks.

461
00:40:19,528 --> 00:40:21,528
Thank you.

462
00:40:23,482 --> 00:40:25,994
Then give me a minute.

463
00:40:38,696 --> 00:40:40,696
Thanks, Seul Ah.

464
00:40:41,303 --> 00:40:44,302
You always drank that.

465
00:40:44,996 --> 00:40:47,126
How did you know?

466
00:40:47,126 --> 00:40:49,126
Because I was a fan.

467
00:40:50,176 --> 00:40:52,366
Actually, not "was."

468
00:40:52,366 --> 00:40:54,899
I'm still a fan.

469
00:40:57,706 --> 00:41:02,914
I started doing deliveries
because I was looking for you.

470
00:41:02,914 --> 00:41:03,963
What?

471
00:41:03,963 --> 00:41:06,053
At first, I wasn't sure it was really you.

472
00:41:06,053 --> 00:41:08,466
But then I knew.

473
00:41:12,436 --> 00:41:17,609
Honestly,
I don't care what you do for a living.

474
00:41:17,609 --> 00:41:20,488
But you never take off that helmet.

475
00:41:22,036 --> 00:41:24,682
That really breaks my heart.

476
00:41:25,476 --> 00:41:30,062
I know you feel guilty
about what happened to the group.

477
00:41:32,218 --> 00:41:35,016
But because of that guilt...

478
00:41:35,016 --> 00:41:38,889
I don't want you to spend your life
hiding like you don't exist.

479
00:41:40,054 --> 00:41:42,652
I've never been ashamed of you.

480
00:41:42,652 --> 00:41:45,698
Not then, and not now.

481
00:41:45,698 --> 00:41:47,544
So...

482
00:41:48,711 --> 00:41:52,091
At least don't hide from fans like me.

483
00:42:47,009 --> 00:42:51,376
I put together a list of spaces
that fit HAN's concept.

484
00:42:53,236 --> 00:42:55,113
The spaces look good.

485
00:42:55,113 --> 00:42:56,526
And the locations are great.

486
00:42:56,526 --> 00:42:59,656
That spot has only hosted global luxury brands,

487
00:42:59,656 --> 00:43:02,037
so there's a lot of competition for the space.

488
00:43:02,037 --> 00:43:04,431
You must've done a lot of legwork.

489
00:43:04,431 --> 00:43:06,431
Not at all.

490
00:43:07,028 --> 00:43:08,934
But...

491
00:43:09,648 --> 00:43:14,767
It gets plenty of traffic,
but I don't think it would draw HAN customers.

492
00:43:14,767 --> 00:43:16,307
Sorry?

493
00:43:17,168 --> 00:43:20,694
Is this everything you prepared for today?

494
00:43:34,421 --> 00:43:36,634
Just a second.

495
00:43:38,081 --> 00:43:44,607
Actually, there is one place
I had in mind outside this list.

496
00:43:55,292 --> 00:43:57,092
Here...

497
00:43:58,038 --> 00:44:00,138
Ikseon-dong.

498
00:44:01,420 --> 00:44:03,490
I looked into why HAN's Paris flagship

499
00:44:03,490 --> 00:44:06,930
isn't on Saint-Honoré,
with all the luxury boutiques,

500
00:44:06,930 --> 00:44:11,508
but in the old streets of Saint-Germain.

501
00:44:11,508 --> 00:44:16,641
It's full of unique cafes,
independent bookstores, and vintage shops.

502
00:44:16,641 --> 00:44:20,368
People with a strong sense
of personal style go there.

503
00:44:20,368 --> 00:44:24,283
So I wondered where
those people would go in Korea.

504
00:44:24,283 --> 00:44:25,726
And?

505
00:44:25,726 --> 00:44:28,506
The HAN customer I picture

506
00:44:28,506 --> 00:44:33,186
likes to walk, browse, and linger,

507
00:44:33,186 --> 00:44:37,925
then choose what speaks to their own taste.

508
00:44:39,376 --> 00:44:43,195
Now this I like.

509
00:44:45,656 --> 00:44:47,179
Good.

510
00:44:47,179 --> 00:44:50,212
Let's look around this area some more.

511
00:44:52,290 --> 00:44:54,143
Yes, ma'am.

512
00:44:59,234 --> 00:45:02,527
My first brand failed too.

513
00:45:02,527 --> 00:45:05,753
So HAN was your second?

514
00:45:06,597 --> 00:45:09,338
I started it with a friend from fashion school.

515
00:45:09,338 --> 00:45:12,205
Our first season did pretty well.

516
00:45:12,205 --> 00:45:14,417
Then what happened?

517
00:45:15,078 --> 00:45:19,861
My partner betrayed me,
and a big corporation took everything.

518
00:45:19,861 --> 00:45:22,378
I had to start over with nothing.

519
00:45:22,378 --> 00:45:24,821
And that became HAN.

520
00:45:27,506 --> 00:45:29,622
That must've been hard.

521
00:45:29,622 --> 00:45:33,210
It was. But it helped me grow.

522
00:45:33,210 --> 00:45:37,817
It showed me what I was capable of.

523
00:45:37,817 --> 00:45:40,633
I realized I'd relied too much
on my partner's instincts.

524
00:45:40,633 --> 00:45:43,530
It wasn't really me who was doing well.

525
00:45:43,530 --> 00:45:47,567
So when I started HAN, I focused on myself.

526
00:45:47,567 --> 00:45:50,363
What I could bring to the table.

527
00:45:50,363 --> 00:45:52,363
What I was good at.

528
00:45:54,150 --> 00:45:57,356
<i>She really is impressive.</i>

529
00:45:59,536 --> 00:46:01,627
What about you?

530
00:46:01,627 --> 00:46:05,989
Do you feel like
you're doing your own thing at APPELLO?

531
00:46:09,523 --> 00:46:14,896
I'm still learning,
but I think I'm slowly finding my way.

532
00:46:18,362 --> 00:46:24,068
Does my history with CEO Kang bother you?

533
00:46:32,463 --> 00:46:36,583
I'd be lying if I said it didn't.

534
00:46:37,323 --> 00:46:38,780
You're honest.

535
00:46:38,780 --> 00:46:40,757
But...

536
00:46:40,757 --> 00:46:43,523
I trust the person I'm with.

537
00:46:47,725 --> 00:46:49,725
Do you?

538
00:47:00,030 --> 00:47:04,683
<i>HAN customers are ultimately drawn
to exclusivity, aren't they?</i>

539
00:47:08,547 --> 00:47:10,762
Hey.

540
00:47:10,762 --> 00:47:13,710
What are you so worried about?

541
00:47:20,253 --> 00:47:23,190
CEO Han seems pretty favorable toward us.

542
00:47:23,190 --> 00:47:25,190
Don't worry too much.

543
00:47:28,509 --> 00:47:30,399
Seong Wook.

544
00:47:30,399 --> 00:47:34,209
SE is saying things way too similar to us.

545
00:47:36,978 --> 00:47:41,849
But anyone in our industry
could land on the same keywords.

546
00:47:41,849 --> 00:47:44,969
Aren't you being too sensitive lately?

547
00:47:47,442 --> 00:47:49,981
I hope that's all it is.

548
00:47:51,315 --> 00:47:53,648
Don't worry about it.

549
00:48:00,829 --> 00:48:03,047
There's nothing to worry about.

550
00:48:03,047 --> 00:48:04,516
Yeah?

551
00:48:08,420 --> 00:48:09,737
Thanks for today.

552
00:48:09,737 --> 00:48:12,020
You worked hard.

553
00:48:12,020 --> 00:48:15,170
Is there anything else I can help you with?

554
00:48:15,170 --> 00:48:18,343
I'm good. I'm meeting someone here.

555
00:48:18,343 --> 00:48:19,726
Get home safe.

556
00:48:19,726 --> 00:48:22,762
Okay. I'll get going.

557
00:48:45,416 --> 00:48:49,349
I should tell him how well I did today.

558
00:48:57,024 --> 00:48:59,934
<i>Your call cannot be completed.
You will be transferred to voicemail.</i>

559
00:48:59,934 --> 00:49:02,504
<i>Charges will apply after the tone.</i>

560
00:49:43,244 --> 00:49:46,670
[Annual Performance Report]
[SE Performance by Business Division]

561
00:49:50,713 --> 00:49:52,236
[SE Illegal Material AE-10]
[SE Internal Audit Report]

562
00:49:52,236 --> 00:49:54,196
[SE Trading Corporate Analysis]

563
00:50:04,854 --> 00:50:09,460
SE spent way too much
on marketing after the platform launch.

564
00:50:10,401 --> 00:50:12,425
They went all in.

565
00:50:12,425 --> 00:50:13,971
How did you get all this?

566
00:50:13,971 --> 00:50:16,248
Through the firm that consulted for SE:ON.

567
00:50:16,248 --> 00:50:19,954
I've been tracking their moves
since before I came to Korea.

568
00:50:21,953 --> 00:50:24,557
SE always operates the same way.

569
00:50:24,557 --> 00:50:28,464
They talk about partnerships and investments,

570
00:50:28,464 --> 00:50:31,710
but all they want is
to take over the other company.

571
00:50:34,451 --> 00:50:36,898
I know from experience.

572
00:50:39,085 --> 00:50:42,011
They tried the same thing with APPELLO.

573
00:50:50,088 --> 00:50:51,944
[Where are you?]

574
00:50:51,944 --> 00:50:53,830
[I'm done with my off-site work]

575
00:51:11,561 --> 00:51:13,367
[Where are you?]
[I'm done with my off-site work]

576
00:51:21,645 --> 00:51:23,995
[CEO Kang Ha Gi, APPELLO]

577
00:51:31,139 --> 00:51:33,979
I can't even call him.

578
00:51:38,465 --> 00:51:40,398
Pathetic.

579
00:51:43,890 --> 00:51:45,597
[Chan oppa]

580
00:51:52,773 --> 00:51:53,983
Hi, oppa.

581
00:51:53,983 --> 00:51:55,909
<i>What are you up to, Da Reum?</i>

582
00:51:56,590 --> 00:51:59,226
Nothing much.

583
00:51:59,226 --> 00:52:01,762
Then want to hear something?

584
00:52:02,729 --> 00:52:04,195
Hear what?

585
00:52:05,316 --> 00:52:07,395
Hold on.

586
00:52:55,084 --> 00:52:56,850
What do you think?

587
00:52:58,328 --> 00:53:00,967
I love it.

588
00:53:01,961 --> 00:53:06,107
It feels... comforting somehow.

589
00:53:09,180 --> 00:53:12,564
I'd been stuck for a while,
but you helped me break through.

590
00:53:12,564 --> 00:53:13,794
Me?

591
00:53:13,794 --> 00:53:18,004
<i>I took your advice and just followed my heart.</i>

592
00:53:20,947 --> 00:53:23,374
"Followed your heart?"

593
00:53:24,760 --> 00:53:27,458
I should've done this sooner.

594
00:53:27,458 --> 00:53:29,458
<i>Thanks, Da Reum.</i>

595
00:53:32,884 --> 00:53:35,543
I can't even do that myself...

596
00:53:36,552 --> 00:53:39,042
And yet I told you to.

597
00:53:39,042 --> 00:53:40,678
<i>Sorry?</i>

598
00:53:42,050 --> 00:53:43,873
Nothing.

599
00:53:43,873 --> 00:53:46,353
Let me hear it when it's finished.

600
00:53:46,353 --> 00:53:49,199
Sorry. I should go.

601
00:54:22,367 --> 00:54:24,913
Want to have a drink with me?

602
00:54:26,765 --> 00:54:28,717
I'll pass.

603
00:54:31,118 --> 00:54:33,489
Not as CEO of APPELLO.

604
00:54:33,489 --> 00:54:38,093
Just as Kang Ha Gi... when can we talk?

605
00:54:39,213 --> 00:54:40,997
Another time.

606
00:54:40,997 --> 00:54:42,893
With Chan there too.

607
00:54:55,464 --> 00:54:57,277
[Missed Call]
[Ms. Nam Da Reum]

608
00:55:16,110 --> 00:55:18,368
<i>Does my history...</i>

609
00:55:18,368 --> 00:55:21,294
<i>with CEO Kang bother you?</i>

610
00:55:23,164 --> 00:55:25,397
<i>But...</i>

611
00:55:25,397 --> 00:55:28,050
<i>I trust the person I'm with.</i>

612
00:55:30,217 --> 00:55:31,577
<i>Do you?</i>

613
00:55:32,308 --> 00:55:35,227
<i>I'm good. I'm meeting someone here.</i>

614
00:56:17,004 --> 00:56:19,004
I know it's late.

615
00:56:19,930 --> 00:56:21,930
I came because I missed you.

616
00:56:30,232 --> 00:56:32,355
What's wrong?

617
00:56:32,355 --> 00:56:34,745
Did something happen?

618
00:56:36,637 --> 00:56:38,236
Yes.

619
00:56:38,850 --> 00:56:40,560
Earlier...

620
00:56:40,560 --> 00:56:43,766
I saw you go into CEO Han's hotel.

621
00:56:47,367 --> 00:56:50,960
Were you with her this whole time?

622
00:56:56,005 --> 00:56:58,782
- It's...
- You didn't tell me,

623
00:56:58,782 --> 00:57:01,363
and I couldn't reach you.

624
00:57:02,224 --> 00:57:05,242
If I hadn't seen you,
I wouldn't have known you were together.

625
00:57:05,242 --> 00:57:08,241
- Don't get the wrong idea.
- Then what am I supposed to think?

626
00:57:15,211 --> 00:57:18,490
I'll explain later.

627
00:57:24,480 --> 00:57:26,480
I'm sorry.

628
00:57:31,804 --> 00:57:33,778
I'm...

629
00:57:34,989 --> 00:57:38,655
I'm your girlfriend.

630
00:57:40,532 --> 00:57:43,485
How am I any different from a stranger?

631
00:57:46,586 --> 00:57:48,492
Ms. Nam...

632
00:57:52,851 --> 00:57:54,851
I'm sorry.

633
00:57:55,725 --> 00:57:58,638
I can't pretend I'm fine right now.

634
00:59:05,623 --> 00:59:07,248
Here's the final presentation deck.

635
00:59:07,248 --> 00:59:08,301
Okay.

636
00:59:08,301 --> 00:59:09,807
[Customer Profiling Report]

637
00:59:19,047 --> 00:59:20,804
This...

638
00:59:20,804 --> 00:59:25,345
This is completely different
from what we discussed.

639
00:59:25,345 --> 00:59:27,901
I leaked that on purpose.

640
00:59:27,901 --> 00:59:29,781
This is the real one.

641
00:59:31,779 --> 00:59:34,745
We had to be careful until the presentation.

642
00:59:36,902 --> 00:59:39,802
Please review it.

643
00:59:39,802 --> 00:59:41,995
Yes, sir.

644
01:00:05,592 --> 01:00:07,598
Hello.

645
01:00:37,233 --> 01:00:39,184
Looks like they had a fight, right?

646
01:00:39,184 --> 01:00:40,663
Isn't this their first fight
since they started dating?

647
01:00:40,663 --> 01:00:43,489
The tension is killing me.

648
01:00:44,429 --> 01:00:47,020
I've got a hunch.

649
01:00:47,020 --> 01:00:48,720
About what now?

650
01:00:48,720 --> 01:00:51,860
What if they're faking it so we don't catch on?

651
01:00:53,453 --> 01:00:55,566
Why?

652
01:00:55,566 --> 01:00:57,262
I'm telling you!

653
01:00:57,262 --> 01:00:59,239
You know I pick up on these things!

654
01:01:06,018 --> 01:01:07,805
Da Reum.

655
01:01:09,212 --> 01:01:10,236
Found you.

656
01:01:10,236 --> 01:01:12,642
Did you come to see me?

657
01:01:12,642 --> 01:01:15,742
Yeah. You wanted to hear the finished fan song.

658
01:01:20,248 --> 01:01:22,944
You sounded down when we talked last time,

659
01:01:22,944 --> 01:01:25,684
so I was worried something might be wrong.

660
01:01:26,680 --> 01:01:27,871
Nothing's wrong.

661
01:01:27,871 --> 01:01:29,647
I'm all right.

662
01:01:30,741 --> 01:01:33,271
Want to hear it in the showroom?
There are speakers in there.

663
01:01:33,271 --> 01:01:34,520
Sure.

664
01:01:39,762 --> 01:01:42,415
- They have Bluetooth, right?
- Yeah.

665
01:01:44,031 --> 01:01:47,597
I don't think they've figured us out yet.

666
01:01:48,540 --> 01:01:51,280
I'm going to be honest with her now.

667
01:03:38,703 --> 01:03:40,566
<i>Even the wording is the same.</i>

668
01:03:40,566 --> 01:03:41,343
<i>This is driving me crazy.</i>

669
01:03:41,343 --> 01:03:43,876
<i>- They copied us word for word.
- Oh my...</i>

670
01:03:43,876 --> 01:03:46,267
<i>I heard CEO Kang called in sick today.</i>

671
01:03:46,267 --> 01:03:50,573
<i>He never misses work, no matter what.</i>

672
01:03:50,573 --> 01:03:53,146
<i>I'll stay by your side till the end.</i>

673
01:03:54,153 --> 01:03:56,063
<i>There are still things I want to do.</i>

674
01:03:56,063 --> 01:03:58,773
<i>We never waited for you.</i>

675
01:03:58,773 --> 01:04:02,026
<i>I didn't want to hide anymore.</i>

676
01:04:02,026 --> 01:04:04,276
<i>This is who I am.</i>

677
01:04:04,276 --> 01:04:08,107
<i>And so is the part of me that likes you.</i>

678
01:04:08,107 --> 01:04:10,107
<i>I wanted you to see that.</i>

